"Synthetic Data

Theoretical(x) = 20 + 1.5*x
Measured(x) = Theoretical(x) + 4*sin(1.2*x)
Power(x) = 6 + 0.25*x^2

sampleData$(x_line; y_line; Theoretical; 0; 10; 101)
sampleData$(x_points; y_points; Measured; 0; 10; 21)
sampleData$(x_power; y_power; Power; 0; 10; 51)

"Plot Configuration
#md off
figure$(performancePlot)
figureSize$(performancePlot; 900; 480)
plot$(performancePlot; x_line; y_line; #d9534f; Design Trend)
scatter$(performancePlot; x_points; y_points; #292b2c; Measurements)
plotY2$(performancePlot; x_power; y_power; #337ab7; Power)
y2Axis$(performancePlot; Power (kW))
hline$(performancePlot; 32; #d9534f; Design Limit)
yBand$(performancePlot; 32; 38; rgba(217,83,79,0.12); Warning Zone)
hoverUnified$(performancePlot)
render$(performancePlot; Performance Comparison; Time (min); Response (mm))
#md on

"Conclusions

'The chart combines calculated series, discrete observations, a secondary response axis, and explicit review limits in one reusable plotting workflow.